---
title: New York Pizza Dough
cuisine: Italian
tags: [main course]
starred: true
---

Makes a 500g 70% hydration dough ball, enough for a 16-inch pizza.

Place @warm water{200 g} in a #bowl and sprinkle in @salt{5g} and @yeast{1g}. Let it sit for ~{5 minutes} until the yeast is dissolved and the water is foamy.

Add @flour{300 g} and knead until the dough comes together. Let it rest for ~{10 minutes}.

Lift and fold the dough over itself a few times, then let it rest for another ~{10 minutes}.

Divide the dough into equal 500g portions and shape into balls. Place the balls into a floured container, cover, and let them rise in the fridge for at least ~{24 hours}.
